{"v":1,"ts":"2026-10-27T20:35:03.302Z","by":"80b0997e-1458-4699-a596-01e149291227","ws":"wks_7a7eb571278e7047","type":"ticket.update","id":"o2.3","status":"closed","closeReason":"done","note":"RESULT: LEAD_IN_SILENCE_SECONDS 2 -> 0.4 in packages/server/src/server/agent/tts-manager.ts (A2DP settle, not SCO link-up). Tests updated: server tts-manager 11/11, app speak-group-static 26/26 green. Zero is the next step after Des's car test — a small lead-in still prevents the first words being swallowed on a fresh A2DP route."}
{"v":1,"ts":"2026-10-27T20:40:24.132Z","by":"80b0997e-1458-4699-a596-01e149291227","ws":"wks_7a7eb571278e7047","type":"ticket.update","id":"o2.5","status":"closed","closeReason":"done","note":"RESULT: audio-engine.native.ts now takes the media path for standalone speak. PCM is wrapped by new pcm16ToWav() at the provider's own rate (24 kHz) and played via expo-audio createAudioPlayer (USAGE_MEDIA, MODE_NORMAL, A2DP) with focus released on completion. The 16 kHz duplex engine is kept only while the mic is active (voice mode, echo reference). Web/desktop already played PCM at its native rate — only the mic-capture path resamples to 16 kHz. Tests: new wav.test.ts 4/4 (RED first), app audio suite 26/26, server tts-manager 11/11, app+server typecheck clean, lint 0 warnings. APK installed on the Pixel at 20:40."}
