{"v":1,"ts":"2026-10-27T21:20:11.351Z","by":"80b0997e-1458-4699-a596-01e149291227","ws":"wks_7a7eb571278e7047","type":"ticket.update","id":"o2.6","status":"closed","closeReason":"done","note":"RESULT: sentences stream. speak-group.ts plays each chunk on arrival in chunkIndex order on ONE session held by playback.hold()/releaseHold() from first chunk to last; onGroupDone is done-guarded so the hold releases exactly once on completion, error and teardown (a leaked hold would be the o4 bug, music never resuming). Per-chunk client.audioPlayed; teardown aborts live groups and the daemon settles on group release. Verified by me, not on the lane's word: read trim/hold/streamer diffs, my own run 64/64 across src/audio + voice-runtime, app+server typecheck clean. Lane flagged one mechanical edit outside its lane: voice-runtime.test.ts mock needed the two new interface methods."}
